'''Gerard C. Ross''' (born December 27, 1982) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player for the [[Seattle Seahawks]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL). He played [[college football]] for the [[Florida State Seminoles football|Florida State Seminoles]]. He was signed by the Seahawks in 2006,<ref>[https://www.espn.com/espn/wire?section=nfl&id=2447852 Seahawks add cornerback, release two offensive linemen]</ref> activated to their active roster in January 2007.<ref>[http://seattletimes.nwsource.com/html/seahawks/2003522937_hawknotes13.html Hawks Notebook | WRs Jackson, Hackett sit out]</ref><ref>[https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=nwQmAAAAIBAJ&sjid=j3QDAAAAIBAJ&pg=4050,956397&dq=gerard-ross+cornerback&hl=en Deal Allows Pacman To Appear, Not Wrestle]</ref> He played in one playoff game for the Seahawks during the 2006 season.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/R/RossGe20.htm | title=Gerard Ross | publisher=[[Pro Football Reference]] | accessdate=27 February 2025}}</ref>

